From e88d62a1e0058dc32643f7f3253cd972fa444235 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Cueto <crcueto25@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:05:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] D4a: DuDe frees the visualization pocket copies of a BPC

PATCH(dude-4a). c_BPC::determineConcavity_real copies the pocket of the
BPC and of each kid with seg2Ply (new vertices, read only for a
visualization that is commented out) and never freed them. They are
destroyed at the end of the function (it has no other return).
LeakSanitizer, H-03 test alone: 1,784,000 B / 11,500 allocations
before, 1,066,400 B / 7,600 after. DudeReference unchanged (own process
and whole program); no ASan or UBSan report.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/bpc.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/bpc.cpp b/src/bpc.cpp
index a2b4eac..da9b0c4 100644
--- a/src/bpc.cpp
+++ b/src/bpc.cpp
@@ -417,6 +417,11 @@ void c_BPC::determineConcavity_real(float tau, bool reducePMs) {
         m_concavities.push_back(*i);
     }
   }
+  // PATCH(dude-4a): the pocket copies made for visualization (seg2Ply, new
+  // vertices nothing else points to) were never freed
+  tmpply.destroy();
+  for (size_t i = 0; i < tmpChildren.size(); i++)
+    tmpChildren[i].destroy();
 }
 void c_BPC::determineConcavity(float tau, bool reducePMs) {
   determineConcavity_real(tau, reducePMs);
